Subject: mysqld.cc: socket pair, not pipe, to wake the listen loop on OpenVMS

handle_connections_sockets() polls the listening sockets together with the
read end of a pipe, which break_connect_loop() writes to on shutdown. On
OpenVMS poll() reports a pipe readable at once, before any write
(probes/poll_wake.c in vms-mariadb); a socketpair() wakes the poll only
when written to, from any thread.

--- a/sql/mysqld.cc	2026-10-05 01:48:51.777611745 -0700
+++ b/sql/mysqld.cc	2026-10-05 01:48:51.900215678 -0700
@@ -6513,7 +6513,15 @@
     set_non_blocking_if_supported(listen_sockets.at(i));
   }
   int termination_fds[2];
+#ifdef __VMS
+  /*
+    On OpenVMS poll() reports a pipe (a mailbox) readable before anything
+    has been written to it; a socket pair behaves as the pipe does elsewhere.
+  */
+  if (socketpair(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0, termination_fds))
+#else
   if (pipe(termination_fds))
+#endif
   {
     sql_print_error("pipe() failed %d", errno);
     DBUG_VOID_RETURN;
